What this change does:

- Before: sublanguage nodes (such as embedded PHP in an HTML-like wrapper) were _not_ prefixed, resulting in `<span class="php">…</span>` and ultimately leaking the bare `php` class into your output.
- After: every token kind is consistently rendered as `<span class="hljs-php">…</span>`, never `<span class="php">…</span>`.  That removes the unwanted bare `php` class.
